  "reviewedPurpose": "Cumulative pure-WLD circuit-world ABI 2 with four-argument begin, bounded retained-pixel query and no sidecar parser/session/source/save or custom color mapping. Default OFF retains vanilla per-TripWire type-445 horizontal/vertical crossing XOR. ON combines device generation dedup with WireHead-style per-pixel different-colour connected-group pair parity at each shared physical gate-wave boundary; incompatible same-colour dual-axis topology rejects ON with TCW_UNSUPPORTED without mutation. This is a restricted pixel rule, not a full WireHead topology emulator or its multi-pixel dictionary-overwrite behavior. Idle switching preserves frames, ROM/RAM, input and RNG. Shared physical gate-wave VM execution remains unchanged. Cold-load compilation enumerates wired/gate rows in original order, uses inline paged DSU accessors and bounds-checked tile reads without duplicate checks; every input tile record remains decoded and validated and temporary row indexes are freed after compilation. Export the four existing incremental SHA-256 functions in the WLD Web profile for bounded native hashing by the host; the existing C hash implementation is byte-identical to the frozen v3 source. Sparse READ_LAMPS queries restore existing 64-column checkpoints only at complete-column boundaries when the next requested point has a later checkpoint, preserve original point order/duplicates, and yield immediately after each restore. Compilation, source validation, viewport, write, trigger, simulation and save semantics are unchanged.",
  "runtimeContract": {
    "circuitWorldAbiVersion": 2,
    "circuitWorldWireHeadPixels": 1,
    "readyReservedBits": {
      "0": "reserved zero",
      "1": "optimization ON",
      "2": "compatible PixelBox topology",
      "3": "ON pixel rule selected"
    },
    "saveReserved": 0,
    "defaultOptimization": false
  },
